    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78-a1">

                <pb facs="0784" n="774" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv05/pg774"/>

                <head>Appendix to CF–21</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-21">May 21, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">extension of time-limit granted
                        to germans</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>; I beg to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    letter of the 20th of May<anchor n="1" xml:id="d78-f1"/> stating that the
                    subjects on which the German Delegation wishes to offer suggestions are so
                    complicated that the memoranda of the German Delegation cannot be completed
                    within the fifteen days granted on the 7th instant and asking in consequence for
                    an extension of the time limit.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to inform Your Excellency that the Allied and Associated
                    Governments are willing to grant an extension until Thursday, May 29th.</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Clemenceau</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herr Brockdorff-Rantzau</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
